## Example incident (anonymised)

A coordinator drafted a task-md citing `SkipTapped` as the user-intent action name. Dev grep'd: no `SkipTapped` in the repo. The actual action was `Skip` (the coordinator had mentally pluralised it from "skip button tapped" thinking). Dev wrote `-block.md`; coordinator re-grep'd, fixed task-md to use `Skip`, re-dispatched. 25 min lost. If the dev had "interpreted" instead of blocking, the fix would have targeted a non-existent handler.
